            Probes were counted twice and independently: by dhcp4.py's own AsyncSniffer and
            by tcpdump into a per-leg pcap. Both ends agree in every leg.

  Method: a ping cannot express any of this case. Each step sends a crafted DHCPDISCOVER
  with a unique chaddr and counts what the DUT puts on the wire in reply. Addresses are
  consumed in order, so each step takes the next free pool address and the assertion is on
  the RELATIONSHIP (probed address == offered address; answered probe => that address
  withheld), never on a hardcoded address. Every positive is paired with a control flow in
  the same run that must NOT produce the same result.

